abstract: >
  Sysmic is a Python framework for precision-calibrated Bayesian fractal
  tomography of seismic catalogs. It implements the Grassberger-Procaccia
  algorithm with MCMC inference of latent dimensionality D3 (emcee, 32
  walkers, 10 000 steps, Uniform[1.5, 3.0] prior), identifying the Fisher
  Information Barrier — the critical precision threshold (σ_c = 2.3 ± 0.4 km)
  beyond which Bayesian inference collapses to the prior. Companion software
  to Firmenich et al. (2026), JGR Solid Earth.
keywords:
  - seismology
  - fractal dimension
  - bayesian inference
  - fisher information
  - grassberger-procaccia
  - hi-net
  - tectonic hierarchy
  - open science
  - emcee
  - MCMC
